  (descr "BXCONN FC-05B40P21H20 (LCSC C23398824), 40-position 0.5mm-pitch dual-contact (top-and-bottom entry, 'no polarity') Flip-Top ZIF FPC connector, SMT right-angle. Hand-authored for pilink-4b6 (required pre-fab swap from the bottom-contact-only AFC01-S40FCA-00/C262674, which cannot mate the display FPC under this project's back-face contact-side working assumption -- see .research/findings/2026-11-15-display-fpc-contact-side.md). Pad pitch (0.5mm) and full 40-position span (DIMA = (N-1)*0.5mm = 19.5mm, pads at -9.75..+9.75mm) are read directly off this part's own CAD drawing (BXCONN dwg BX-CN-001-A, 'FC-05BNP21H20', title '0.5 Pitch H2.0 Backflip R/A Type CONN'), recovered in this environment by hand-decompressing the datasheet PDF's Flate-compressed content stream (no PDF rasterizer installed) and replaying its vector path/bezier operators with a small purpose-built interpreter -- not transcribed from a thumbnail. The drawing's own recommended-PCB-footprint detail additionally gives pad width 0.35mm+/-0.05 (X, used here in place of a guess) and confirms the 2.00mm 'Height Above Board' JLCPCB catalog field (section A-A). Pad Y-length (1.3mm), the Y pad-row offset (2.68mm), the body/courtyard Y-profile, and the MP1/MP2 mounting-pad size/offset are NOT independently sourced from this drawing (its mounting-pad/body-depth dimensions could not be confidently disambiguated from the recovered vector geometry in the time available) -- they are reused as placeholders from this project's existing AFC01-S40FCA-00 footprint (same pitch/position-count connector class, similar overall size: this part's own DIMB formula (N+8)*0.5+0.02 = 24.02mm overall width is close to that footprint's 24.4mm), same convention as that footprint's own original bootstrapping. Needs a human KiCad-GUI DRC/visual pass before fab, same caveat class as every other hand-authored footprint in this project. PIN-1 PHYSICAL LOCATION CAVEAT (pilink-4b6, load-bearing, do not drop on edit): this footprint places pad 1 at the LEFT end (x=-9.75) and pad 40 at the right, identical to the AFC01-S40FCA-00 footprint it replaces, so the schematic's existing pin/net mapping is carried over UNCHANGED (no reversal applied). This was NOT verified against a real part: AFC01-S40FCA-00's own LCSC-hosted datasheet (C262674.pdf) is confirmed (independently re-checked for this bead, not just inherited from the prior finding) to be a generic 29-page Jushuo reliability/process booklet with a placeholder 'AFC01-S**FCA-00' watermark and no dimensioned drawing at all -- so there is no primary source to compare this part's own confirmed NO.1 location (this drawing's section-A/A1 views, next to the 'A' datum triangle) against. If a real sample of both connectors (or a proper Jushuo drawing) later shows their NO.1 ends don't correspond the way this footprint assumes, J501's pin-to-net mapping in display.kicad_sch must be reversed, not just this footprint swapped -- flag any such finding against this placeholder before fab.")
